 "rootCauses": [
  "Images with managed surfaces store every TS list as the foundation SparseList. As an AVL tree that is one node per element, an O(log2 n) pointer walk per read and a rebalancing insert per push. Symbolized 24-eval fixture on main: readList 32.6% exclusive, AVL insert/balance/height ~9%.",
  "lowerReferenceLists ran under a fixed 10M-unit budget. The native compiler image already used 8.83M on main, so the slightly larger trie IR made it decline silently: 59.8 MB stage1 instead of 46.6 MB, and all 365 sparse instantiations retained.",
  "Typed-array element stores test CanonicalNumericIndexString by a stringToNumber + shortest-digits numberToString round-trip per key; bignum digit generation was ~12% of copyWithin coerced-values."
 ],
 "rejected": [
  "hashString four code units per ToUint32: neutral in matched A/B on main (decodeURI 159.5 vs 161.2, New_Tai_Lue 24.6 vs 24.6 CPU-s) and on main+J (87.4 vs 89.3, 14.7 vs 14.7); dropped from the slice.",
  "Compare-based inline readList: +2.7 KB per specialization and 17% slower on New_Tai_Lue."
 ],
 "design": "Header {length, root} and the bound list methods are unchanged, so closed programs still lower to dense lists. Leaves hold 8 values plus a presence mask (holes stay distinct from stored undefined). Branches hold 8 children plus a count. The root shift bounds the indices it covers. Emptied nodes are pruned. Truncation visits only existing nodes. ",
